# The first fix from the 2026-11-07 night: the centroid never sat on
# Saturn, in focus or out of it, because the search keyed on the single
# brightest pixel and at gain 353 that is a hot pixel. This renders a
# dim Saturn on a noisy, hot-pixelled frame -- what the real sensor gave
# -- and asks for the whole acquisition to lock.
#
# Pointed at Kochab, which is in the tracking band at any hour at this
# site (see motion.scn); RADUK_EMU_TARGET makes the emulator draw Saturn
# there whatever the profile says.
name    Search: lock on a dim planet among hot pixels
timeout 300

env     RADUK_EMU_TARGET=Saturn
env     RADUK_EMU_NOISE=12
env     RADUK_EMU_HOT_PIXELS=600
env     RADUK_EMU_PEAK_DN=70
profile star.ini focuser position=168000

expect 30  [SCENARIO] Search
wait   3
goto   Kochab
expect 120 SEARCHING
expect 30  Search: target at
absent 1   Search: nothing found
wait   3
shot   searching
press  PLANET LOCK
expect 120 Acquisition: Locked
wait   3
shot   locked
